  "body": "Fixes https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5496. \n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium\n   * Firefox\n   * Safari\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   - Tentative tests can be found at https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/tree/master/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element. Here's what we still need:\n   - [x] Test that the a deferred iframe is fetched with the referrer policy computed at load-deferral time\n   - [x] Test that a deferred iframe is fetched with a URL that was parsed against\n   - [x] Test generic lazy load behavior (i.e., below-viewport `loading=lazy` iframes do not load)\n   - [x] Test generic lazy load eager behavior\n   - [x] Test loading=lazy on srcdoc iframes\n   - [x] Test that below-viewport `loading=lazy` iframes can be lazy loaded multiple times, and that a document in an iframe isn't unloaded until the second time the `ready to be lazy loaded` flag is loaded\n   - [x] From discussion with @annevk, test that setting `loading=eager` and then immediately removing the attribute still continues the load (we need this for images too)\n   - [x] Test that setting `loading=eager` on a deferred iframe correctly sets the `ready to be lazy loaded flag` and continues the load\n   - [x] Test that in-viewport loading=lazy iframes do not block the outer window load event\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/master/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chrome: N/A\n   * Firefox: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1622090\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=196698\n\nAside: One thing I noticed about https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5510 is that I think it didn't fully fix https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5236. I think it's still weird that we're waiting in parallel for the `ready to be lazy loaded` bool to be mutated on the main thread, and then we queue a task from in-parallel to continue. IMO one of the big wins of using an IntersectionObserver is that we can use the callback to just synchronously finish the loading right from there. I'll start another thread with my latest proposed design to fix this, but for now, the iframe spec behaves similar to images.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/embedded-content.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">/embedded-content.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/4db63e0...d781928/embedded-content.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/iframe-embed-object.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">/iframe-embed-object.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/4db63e0...d781928/iframe-embed-object.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">/images.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/4db63e0...d781928/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/4db63e0...d781928/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/urls-and-fetching.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">/urls-and-fetching.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5579/4db63e0...d781928/urls-and-fetching.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 1, 2020, 4:44 PM UTC (d781928)\">diff</a> )",
